WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.338 --> 00:00:04.638
Still think this is destiny?

2
00:00:04.798 --> 00:00:06.438
- Hank, we have to find my folks!
- Quiet!

3
00:00:13.014 --> 00:00:16.394
Ugh. Base, this is Carol.

4
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.680
Uh, I think I might have found
that missing octopus. Over.

5
00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.060
- See what you did?
- Sorry.

6
00:00:22.232 --> 00:00:23.562
This could not be worse.

7
00:00:23.733 --> 00:00:27.903
Hmm. "Destiny." Destiny.

8
00:00:28.071 --> 00:00:30.701
- Hank. I got a feeling.
- Sh!

9
00:00:30.824 --> 00:00:32.009
I think we should get in the bucket.

10
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.203
- No. Stop.
- Seriously. It says "destiny" and it is...

11
00:00:34.369 --> 00:00:36.013
- No, no, no, no, no.
- We've got to get in that bucket.

12
00:00:36.037 --> 00:00:40.337
- I'm not going with you in that bucket.
- Here... I... go... in... the... bucket. Bye.

13
00:00:42.752 --> 00:00:47.552
Hey, guys, I'm looking for my family.
Oh, good idea. Play dead.

14
00:00:54.264 --> 00:00:57.644
I'm sorry. I got to blink. How do you
hold your eyes open that long?

15
00:01:08.904 --> 00:01:11.944
Hey, guys. Wait a second.

16
00:01:18.997 --> 00:01:21.757
Our next guest
has been here a very long time.

17
00:01:21.917 --> 00:01:25.927
She's a whale shark.
Her name is Destiny.

18
00:01:26.046 --> 00:01:27.296
Destiny? Really?

19
00:01:27.422 --> 00:01:30.462
You'll notice she's extremely
near-sighted and has trouble...

20
00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:34.884
navigating her environment.
Oh! And here she comes now.

21
00:01:35.013 --> 00:01:38.513
Ooh! Destiny. You're a fish?

22
00:01:40.393 --> 00:01:41.853
Wait. What?

23
00:01:41.978 --> 00:01:44.988
- Hi! Hello there.
- Whoa! Oh. Whoa.

24
00:01:46.441 --> 00:01:48.111
All right, I'll go with you.

25
00:01:48.985 --> 00:01:52.445
- Excuse me.
- Is that blue blob talking?

26
00:01:52.572 --> 00:01:54.952
- Can you help me? I lost my family.
- You lost your family?

27
00:01:55.116 --> 00:01:56.366
Well, it's a long story,

28
00:01:56.451 --> 00:01:58.262
and truth be told,
I don't remember most of it.

29
00:01:58.286 --> 00:02:00.046
Aw, that is so sad.
You poor thi...

30
00:02:03.291 --> 00:02:06.621
Sorry. Not a great swimmer.
I can't see very well.

31
00:02:06.795 --> 00:02:08.215
Oh, I think you swim beautifully.

32
00:02:08.296 --> 00:02:10.416
In fact, I've never seen a fish
swim like that before.

33
00:02:10.465 --> 00:02:12.175
Thank you.

34
00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.800
You're welcome.

35
00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.090
Wait. Say that again.

36
00:02:16.221 --> 00:02:19.141
Um, you're welcome.

37
00:02:19.307 --> 00:02:20.817
- Dory?
- Yes.

38
00:02:20.976 --> 00:02:21.976
- Dory?
- Yes.

39
00:02:22.102 --> 00:02:23.102
- Dory?
- Yes.

40
00:02:23.186 --> 00:02:24.776
- Dory!
- Yes.

41
00:02:24.896 --> 00:02:27.066
- You and I were friends!
- No!

42
00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.150
- Dory, it's me! Destiny!
- You know me?

43
00:02:29.317 --> 00:02:31.987
Of course! We talked through the pipes
when we were little.

44
00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:33.783
- We were pipe pals!
- We were?

45
00:02:34.364 --> 00:02:37.204
- Aw, you're so pretty.
- So you know where I'm from?

46
00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:39.247
Yep, you are from
the Open Ocean exhibit.

47
00:02:39.744 --> 00:02:41.164
I'm from the Open Ocean exhibit?

48
00:02:41.329 --> 00:02:42.929
Then that's
where my parents are.

49
00:02:42.998 --> 00:02:44.392
We got to go. Can you take me there?

50
00:02:44.416 --> 00:02:47.086
Uh... Kind of tough for a whale
to travel around here.

51
00:02:47.252 --> 00:02:50.542
Can you please keep it down
over there? My head hurts.

52
00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:51.691
Who's that?

53
00:02:51.715 --> 00:02:52.817
That's my neighbour, Bailey.

54
00:02:52.841 --> 00:02:54.318
He was brought in with a head injury.

55
00:02:54.342 --> 00:02:55.569
I know you're talking about me, Destiny.

56
00:02:55.593 --> 00:02:57.863
He thinks he can't use his echolocation,
but I've overheard...

57
00:02:57.887 --> 00:03:00.074
the doctors talking.
There's not a thing wrong with him.

58
00:03:00.098 --> 00:03:02.018
Hear every word
you're saying about me.

59
00:03:02.142 --> 00:03:03.182
What's echolocation?

60
00:03:03.351 --> 00:03:06.271
Bailey's head is supposed to put out
a call and the echo helps him...

61
00:03:06.438 --> 00:03:11.488
find objects far away.
Oh, but apparently he's still "healing."

62
00:03:11.609 --> 00:03:13.439
Now I know you're talking about me.

63
00:03:13.528 --> 00:03:15.368
- I really can't echolocate.
- Oh.

64
00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.383
I cannot have this conversation again.
I just can't.

65
00:03:17.407 --> 00:03:20.457
I hit my head very hard out there.
See how swollen it is!

66
00:03:20.618 --> 00:03:22.918
Your head is supposed to be big!
You're a beluga!

67
00:03:23.079 --> 00:03:24.829
Echolocation.

68
00:03:24.914 --> 00:03:27.464
Oh, like the world's
most powerful pair of glasses?

69
00:03:27.542 --> 00:03:28.712
- What?
- What are glasses?

70
00:03:28.835 --> 00:03:30.625
It's sort of like you go, "hoo"

71
00:03:30.712 --> 00:03:33.502
and then you see things.
Why do I know that?

72
00:03:33.631 --> 00:03:36.051
Oh. That's interesting.

73
00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.430
There you are!
Listen up, you and I are square.

74
00:03:41.598 --> 00:03:44.108
I took you to the map,
now give me that tag!

75
00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.454
Wait, no. I know where my parents are.
They're in the...

76
00:03:46.478 --> 00:03:49.318
What's it called? The place...
The soap and lotion?

77
00:03:49.481 --> 00:03:51.151
- Open Ocean.
- Open Ocean!

78
00:03:51.316 --> 00:03:53.776
Open Ocean!
I know where that is.

79
00:03:53.943 --> 00:03:57.073
That's the exhibit located right next to...
I don't care.

80
00:03:57.238 --> 00:03:58.078
Easy!

81
00:03:58.156 --> 00:04:01.076
If you're trying to get to the Open Ocean
exhibit go through the pipes.

82
00:04:01.242 --> 00:04:03.452
- Through the pipes. Great.
- Through the pipes?

83
00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:05.700
Yep. Take two lefts, swim straight
and you'll hit it.

84
00:04:05.789 --> 00:04:09.869
Oh, that's a lot of directions. That's...
Did you get that, Hank? All that?

85
00:04:10.001 --> 00:04:11.921
- Uh, yeah.
- Great! Let's go.

86
00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.500
I'm not going with you. I won't fit.
You have to go by yourself.

87
00:04:16.174 --> 00:04:17.174
Um...

88
00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:24.300
That's... I'm... I... See, I can't because
I'm not so good with directions.

89
00:04:24.474 --> 00:04:27.524
Well, that's too bad. A deal's a deal.
You wanted to find your parents?

90
00:04:27.685 --> 00:04:29.645
That's how you get to them.
Now give me your tag.

91
00:04:29.813 --> 00:04:32.653
But, Hank, I can't go in the pipes alone.
I'll forget where I'm going.

92
00:04:32.774 --> 00:04:35.694
- Not my problem. Tag!
- But I can't get in that way.

93
00:04:35.819 --> 00:04:38.819
- I'm sorry, but there's no other way.
- There's no other way.

94
00:04:40.782 --> 00:04:44.122
- There's no other way.
- Now, now. Don't panic.

95
00:04:44.285 --> 00:04:48.335
It's okay. Not everything in life is
easy to do. Isn't that right, Charlie?

96
00:04:48.498 --> 00:04:52.628
She's right. When something's
too hard, you should just give up.

97
00:04:52.794 --> 00:04:54.714
- Charlie!
- A joke. I'm kidding!

98
00:04:54.879 --> 00:04:58.499
Just a joke. A joke.
Caution, joker at work.

99
00:04:58.675 --> 00:05:00.111
Joke. I got it.

100
00:05:00.135 --> 00:05:03.305
You see, kelpcake?
There's always another way.

101
00:05:05.348 --> 00:05:06.858
Thank you, Daddy.

102
00:05:08.143 --> 00:05:09.643
Thank you, Daddy.

103
00:05:09.727 --> 00:05:12.317
Nope. My father said
there's always another way.

104
00:05:12.397 --> 00:05:15.987
- What? There is no other way.
- Open Ocean. Open Ocean. Hmm...

105
00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:19.237
Open Ocean. I'm pretty sure
it's the building over there.

106
00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:22.570
That's ill-defined and roundish.
Like Bailey's head.

107
00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:24.700
- Wait, what?
- Always another way. There's...

108
00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:28.838
There! Guys, follow me.
I know how we can get to locomotion.

109
00:05:28.997 --> 00:05:30.337
Open Ocean.
Exactly.

110
00:05:31.082 --> 00:05:34.672
Um, guys.
You know I can't swim over there, right?

111
00:05:35.587 --> 00:05:38.347
Ooo-roo, ooo-roo, ooo-roo.

112
00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:40.750
I don't see how this
is going to get us inside.

113
00:05:40.842 --> 00:05:42.092
What are you even doing?

114
00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:44.010
We're calling her over, of course.

115
00:05:44.179 --> 00:05:45.929
Calling her over? Calling who over?

116
00:05:50.602 --> 00:05:52.772
Lads, meet Becky.

117
00:05:54.856 --> 00:05:58.616
Flying? No, no, no new information.

118
00:05:58.776 --> 00:06:00.236
Listen, tell her thank you.

119
00:06:00.361 --> 00:06:02.531
You guys have gone
above and beyond. Really.

120
00:06:02.697 --> 00:06:06.917
But is there a way to get in
that involves, like, swimming?

121
00:06:07.076 --> 00:06:08.476
Because that's really our strength.

122
00:06:08.536 --> 00:06:11.166
Look, your friend is going to be
in quarantine.

123
00:06:11.289 --> 00:06:13.199
That's where they take the sick fish.

124
00:06:13.458 --> 00:06:16.968
And the one and only one way
into that place is Becky.

125
00:06:20.089 --> 00:06:21.499
Hi, Becky.

126
00:06:21.591 --> 00:06:24.421
Ow! Stop. Let's call
her Pecky because this is hurting.

127
00:06:24.594 --> 00:06:26.071
I think she likes you, Dad.

128
00:06:26.095 --> 00:06:31.065
Becky, love? These two nice fish
need to get into quarantine.

129
00:06:31.226 --> 00:06:33.066
Are you free today, Rebecca darling?

130
00:06:33.186 --> 00:06:36.946
Becky, is... Would that work
with your schedule? Ow!

131
00:06:37.106 --> 00:06:38.856
She doesn't understand
what I'm saying.

132
00:06:38.983 --> 00:06:41.573
All you have to do
is imprint with her, mate.

133
00:06:41.694 --> 00:06:43.324
- Imp... What?
- Imprint.

134
00:06:43.488 --> 00:06:47.578
Look her in the eye and say, "ooo-roo"
and she'll be in sync with you.

135
00:06:47.742 --> 00:06:50.822
- Now look her in the eye.
- Yeah.

136
00:06:50.912 --> 00:06:54.912
Nemo, I think we should
devise an alternate plan.

137
00:06:55.083 --> 00:06:57.753
One that involves staying in the water
and someone sane.

138
00:06:57.919 --> 00:07:00.959
Because this bird, this bird...
This ain't the bird!

139
00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:03.920
That's fine, Dad. And in the meantime,
Dory will just forget us.

140
00:07:04.092 --> 00:07:05.972
Like you said, it's what she does best.

141
00:07:06.135 --> 00:07:07.765
Fine.

142
00:07:09.097 --> 00:07:10.187
Uh...

143
00:07:10.265 --> 00:07:14.725
Okay, look her in the eye. Which eye?

144
00:07:14.852 --> 00:07:16.102
Just pick one, mate.

145
00:07:16.271 --> 00:07:17.271
Becky.

146
00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:20.190
Uh...

147
00:07:22.443 --> 00:07:27.073
Ooh. Ooo-roo.
Roo-roo, Becky.

148
00:07:29.826 --> 00:07:32.326
Okay, this is all great.

149
00:07:33.788 --> 00:07:36.708
How exactly is Becky
supposed to carry us?

150
00:07:36.833 --> 00:07:40.623
Oh yeah. I almost forgot. Gerald!

151
00:07:40.795 --> 00:07:42.385
- Hmm?
- Yeah, Gerald.

152
00:07:42.547 --> 00:07:43.967
- Come on, son.
- Hmm?

153
00:07:44.674 --> 00:07:48.974
Come on, Gerald. Give us your pail,
we'll let you sit on the rock.

154
00:07:49.137 --> 00:07:51.807
- Yeah, Gerald. We swear it.
- Hmm.

155
00:07:53.641 --> 00:07:56.391
That's right. Shimmy on over here.

156
00:07:56.561 --> 00:07:58.561
Come on. You can do it.

157
00:07:59.314 --> 00:08:00.394
That's right.

158
00:08:00.565 --> 00:08:02.025
Mind you don't scuff your bum.

159
00:08:04.819 --> 00:08:07.569
Thank you so much, Gerald.

160
00:08:07.739 --> 00:08:10.359
Welcome to your time on this rock.

161
00:08:11.909 --> 00:08:13.529
Comfortable, isn't it?

162
00:08:14.662 --> 00:08:15.912
Time's up! Get off!

163
00:08:15.997 --> 00:08:17.850
- Off! Off! Off! Off!
- Time's up! Now get off, Gerald! Off!

164
00:08:17.874 --> 00:08:22.464
No, this is nuts! Why do I keep getting
talked into insane choices?

165
00:08:22.587 --> 00:08:23.747
Good luck!

166
00:08:28.426 --> 00:08:30.056
Okay, when I tell you you're gonna...

167
00:08:30.219 --> 00:08:32.139
Yeah. I know. I'm gonna signal
with a big splash.

168
00:08:32.263 --> 00:08:36.353
On my mark. Not clear yet.
Not clear yet.

169
00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:39.560
- Now?
- Not 'til Destiny gives the signal.

170
00:08:41.105 --> 00:08:44.235
You know something? I have no idea
why you're even doing this.

171
00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:46.190
What do you mean?

172
00:08:46.361 --> 00:08:48.339
It seems like a lot of trouble
just to find some more fish.

173
00:08:48.363 --> 00:08:50.193
If I had short-term memory loss...

174
00:08:50.365 --> 00:08:52.343
I'd just swim off into the blue
and forget everything.

175
00:08:52.367 --> 00:08:54.178
Well I don't want to do that.
I want my family.

176
00:08:54.202 --> 00:08:56.242
Not me, kid. I don't want anyone
to worry about.

177
00:08:56.788 --> 00:09:00.708
You're lucky. No memories.
No problems.

178
00:09:00.875 --> 00:09:03.795
Huh. No memories. No problems.

179
00:09:04.045 --> 00:09:07.295
Still not clear. Still not clear.

180
00:09:07.465 --> 00:09:08.942
You don't have to say when it's not time.

181
00:09:08.966 --> 00:09:10.444
- Not...
- Just tell me when it is time.

182
00:09:10.468 --> 00:09:12.228
Okay, here we go. And... Wait!

183
00:09:12.386 --> 00:09:14.186
"Here we go. Wait."
Are you serious?

184
00:09:14.222 --> 00:09:15.949
- Okay, on the count of three.
- Don't count. Just say, "Go."

185
00:09:15.973 --> 00:09:18.254
- Go! Now, now. Do it! Do it!
- What? Okay, okay.

186
00:09:18.309 --> 00:09:20.599
- Wow. Look at that! I mean...
- That's the signal.

187
00:09:20.728 --> 00:09:22.648
Go, go, go! That's the signal!

188
00:09:27.568 --> 00:09:30.328
Now remember,
Destiny said follow the signs

189
00:09:30.404 --> 00:09:32.124
- to the Open Ocean exhibit.
- Uh-huh.

190
00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:35.740
I can't see squat,
so it's your job to look for it.

191
00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:37.740
Got it. Follow the signs to Open Ocean.

192
00:09:37.912 --> 00:09:39.598
I'm just gonna repeat it, okay?
That should work.

193
00:09:39.622 --> 00:09:42.122
Follow the signs to Open Ocean.
Follow the signs to Open Ocean.

194
00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:45.330
Mm. Go right! Follow the signs
to Open Ocean.

195
00:09:45.503 --> 00:09:48.923
Follow the signs to Open Ocean.
Follow the signs to Open Ocean. Left!

196
00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:51.151
- Follow the signs to Open Ocean.
- And steer clear of people, will you?

197
00:09:51.175 --> 00:09:53.345
Especially kids.
I don't want to be touched.

198
00:09:53.427 --> 00:09:54.977
Sh! Do not mess me up!

199
00:09:57.598 --> 00:10:01.018
Oh, poor baby.
Let me get that for you. Here you... Oh!

200
00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:03.600
Oh my. Ugh.

201
00:10:04.689 --> 00:10:06.609
Where do we go? Where do we go?

202
00:10:06.774 --> 00:10:09.654
Oh, sorry!
Okay, I was looking, looking...

203
00:10:09.819 --> 00:10:12.569
Roo-roo, Becky!
Drop us anywhere. We're okay.

204
00:10:12.697 --> 00:10:15.827
Just wait, Dad. I think she's looking
for a place to land.

205
00:10:15.992 --> 00:10:19.662
She's confused, Nemo. She doesn't
even know which way to look.

206
00:10:26.127 --> 00:10:29.847
Wait, Becky. What are you doing?
Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo-roo-roo-roo.

207
00:10:31.716 --> 00:10:35.136
Okay. I was going somewhere.
The question is where.

208
00:10:35.303 --> 00:10:36.973
Which way? Do you see the sign?

209
00:10:37.138 --> 00:10:40.558
I'm looking. I'm looking. Something to
something gets me to my family!

210
00:10:40.725 --> 00:10:43.275
"The world's most powerful pair of..."

211
00:10:43.394 --> 00:10:46.394
I know that. Why do I know that?
It's another memory.

212
00:10:46.564 --> 00:10:49.194
Hank, we need to go that way!
Left. Go left.

213
00:10:53.321 --> 00:10:55.611
Becky! Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo.

214
00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:57.990
She can't hear you, Dad.

215
00:10:58.117 --> 00:11:01.997
All right. New plan. We have to get
closer to Becky so she can hear us.

216
00:11:02.997 --> 00:11:05.077
I don't think we should move the pail.

217
00:11:05.458 --> 00:11:09.008
Nemo. Without me Becky's lost.

218
00:11:09.503 --> 00:11:11.173
Dad, just trust her.

219
00:11:11.255 --> 00:11:14.215
Trust her? So she can forget us
all together?

220
00:11:14.383 --> 00:11:18.013
- I trust Becky.
- You trust her? Becky's eating a cup!

221
00:11:20.014 --> 00:11:23.354
Becky! Becky! Ooo-roo! Whoa!

222
00:11:26.687 --> 00:11:28.197
Ah.

223
00:11:32.568 --> 00:11:34.688
Well, at least we're not stuck
in the bucket any more.

224
00:11:39.075 --> 00:11:40.705
Or on top of quarantine.

225
00:11:41.994 --> 00:11:43.597
The baby otter talk
is beginning now.

226
00:11:43.621 --> 00:11:48.041
Why, thanks, Sigourney Weaver.
Hey, who wants to learn about otters?

227
00:11:49.293 --> 00:11:51.653
Looking for the world's
most powerful pair of glasses.

228
00:11:51.879 --> 00:11:53.039
Otters!

229
00:11:53.214 --> 00:11:55.574
- Welcome, it's a huge cuddle party!
- Cuddle party! I'm in!

230
00:11:57.551 --> 00:12:00.221
Where are we?
Are we close to Open Ocean?

231
00:12:00.388 --> 00:12:02.908
Uh, yes. I think... Well, I don't know.
But I saw that other sign so...

232
00:12:02.932 --> 00:12:03.932
What? What other sign?

233
00:12:04.058 --> 00:12:05.535
The world's most powerful
pair of glasses.

234
00:12:05.559 --> 00:12:08.269
What? What are you talking about?
Why would we follow that sign?

235
00:12:08.396 --> 00:12:10.606
Well, because I remembered it.

236
00:12:10.731 --> 00:12:12.481
No. That wasn't the plan. Ow!

237
00:12:14.568 --> 00:12:17.488
All right, that's it!
You have wasted my time!

238
00:12:17.571 --> 00:12:19.651
- Wait. No.
- That transport truck leaves at dawn...

239
00:12:19.824 --> 00:12:21.614
and I'm not missing it,
so give me your tag.

240
00:12:21.784 --> 00:12:23.244
Wait. No, I remembered that sign.

241
00:12:23.411 --> 00:12:24.991
- So?
- So I'm remembering more...

242
00:12:25.079 --> 00:12:27.557
and more and I feel like my memory's
getting better. I think we should...

243
00:12:27.581 --> 00:12:30.251
No! Your memory is not working.
You can't remember anything.

244
00:12:30.418 --> 00:12:33.088
It's probably how you lost your family
in the first place!

245
00:12:35.965 --> 00:12:39.845
All right, look, let's just take it down
a notch. Just give me the tag and...

246
00:12:40.011 --> 00:12:43.261
You know something, for a guy
with three hearts you're not very nice.

247
00:12:43.431 --> 00:12:45.701
Three hearts? What are you talking
about? I don't have three hearts.

248
00:12:45.725 --> 00:12:46.895
- Yes, you do.
- I don't!

249
00:12:46.976 --> 00:12:47.766
- You do!
- Don't!

250
00:12:47.935 --> 00:12:49.065
- Do!
- Stop saying that!

251
00:12:49.186 --> 00:12:52.316
Fun fact-the octopus has three hearts.

252
00:12:52.398 --> 00:12:54.608
Two pump blood to the gills
while the third pumps...

253
00:12:54.734 --> 00:12:56.128
- blood throughout the body.
- Wait!

254
00:12:56.152 --> 00:12:57.442
Whoa!

255
00:13:00.114 --> 00:13:02.050
You know, someone with three hearts
shouldn't be so mean.

256
00:13:02.074 --> 00:13:04.534
And it's mean to say that
I would lose someone I love!

257
00:13:05.745 --> 00:13:09.045
I did not lose them! Hank?

258
00:13:10.374 --> 00:13:13.004
Hank? Hank?

259
00:13:13.544 --> 00:13:16.464
- Han-s.
- No. Not Hans. I'm looking for Hank.

260
00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:18.800
- Han-s.
- Hank. With a "k." Hank.

261
00:13:18.966 --> 00:13:22.096
- Hands!
- Hands? Oh, oh, oh, hands!

262
00:13:25.181 --> 00:13:27.761
Hank! Hank?

263
00:13:27.892 --> 00:13:28.892
My arm!

264
00:13:28.934 --> 00:13:29.644
Hank!

265
00:13:32.646 --> 00:13:34.146
Where are you? Hank!

266
00:13:34.231 --> 00:13:36.941
Oh! Ahh! Can you please help me?
I'm looking for...

267
00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:41.631
Please help me. I've lost
my friend Frank. I'm sorry, not Frank.

268
00:13:41.655 --> 00:13:42.815
You're in my space!

269
00:13:43.407 --> 00:13:46.207
He's an octopus. No, septo...
Septopus. That's right.

270
00:13:46.368 --> 00:13:48.958
He's a septopus. Septopus.
Septopus. Septopus.

271
00:13:49.038 --> 00:13:52.048
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, s...
Septopus! He's camouflaged!

272
00:13:55.169 --> 00:13:57.419
Hank. Come on, Hank!
Let's get out of here.

273
00:13:57.588 --> 00:13:59.178
Dory, what are you doing?

274
00:13:59.673 --> 00:14:03.053
Hank!
What's the plan?

275
00:14:03.219 --> 00:14:05.339
The plan is I'm gonna stay here forever.

276
00:14:05.513 --> 00:14:06.803
Okay. Good plan.

277
00:14:09.099 --> 00:14:12.389
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, Hank. I'm sorry.
I can't remember right.

278
00:14:13.145 --> 00:14:15.145
- Sweetie. Sweetie.
- Oh, watch out, kelpcake.

279
00:14:15.272 --> 00:14:16.522
Oh, watch where you're going.

280
00:14:17.399 --> 00:14:21.729
I'm sorry, Daddy.
I'm sorry I can't remember right.

281
00:14:21.862 --> 00:14:26.362
Oh, sweetie.
Sweetie, you don't need to be sorry.

282
00:14:26.534 --> 00:14:30.954
You know what you need to do?
Just keep swimming.

283
00:14:31.121 --> 00:14:32.121
Yeah.

284
00:14:32.289 --> 00:14:35.409
And I bet you can remember
that because we're just...

285
00:14:35.876 --> 00:14:36.876
Um...

286
00:14:36.961 --> 00:14:38.381
We're gonna sing a song about it.

287
00:14:38.546 --> 00:14:41.386
Just keep swimming
Just keep swimming

288
00:14:41.549 --> 00:14:44.089
Just keep swimming
Swimming, swimming

289
00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:46.130
What do we do?
We swim

290
00:14:46.303 --> 00:14:49.223
Swim, swim, swim
We swim

291
00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:51.970
- We swim, swim, swim
- Just keep swimming

292
00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:56.690
My parents
taught me that song!

293
00:14:56.772 --> 00:14:58.142
We sang it as a family.

294
00:14:58.315 --> 00:14:59.795
All this time I thought I made it up!

295
00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.570
- What song?
- Just keep swimming.

296
00:15:01.735 --> 00:15:03.735
Hank, we've just got to keep swimming.

297
00:15:03.904 --> 00:15:07.204
What? No way! Listen to me,
it's too dangerous to move.

298
00:15:07.324 --> 00:15:10.164
No, you listen to me. I know
you're scared, but you can't give up.

299
00:15:10.286 --> 00:15:11.326
Follow me.

300
00:15:11.495 --> 00:15:13.955
Just keep swimming
Just keep swimming

301
00:15:15.082 --> 00:15:17.502
My mom wrote
this song for me

302
00:15:18.627 --> 00:15:20.427
It's gonna get us out of here

303
00:15:20.588 --> 00:15:22.008
Sing with me, Hank. Come on.

304
00:15:22.339 --> 00:15:24.959
I'm coming, Mommy.
I'm coming, Daddy!

305
00:15:25.092 --> 00:15:26.762
- We're gonna be okay.
- Stop!

306
00:15:26.927 --> 00:15:28.307
- Huh?
- Turn back.

307
00:15:28.429 --> 00:15:29.629
Turn back!

308
00:15:29.805 --> 00:15:32.685
You're headed
right for Poker's Cove.

309
00:15:32.766 --> 00:15:34.646
Poker's Cove.

310
00:15:35.352 --> 00:15:37.482
- Poker's Cove?
- Incoming!

311
00:15:40.608 --> 00:15:42.118
Stop it!

312
00:15:42.276 --> 00:15:43.776
Oh, what is this?

313
00:15:47.948 --> 00:15:48.788
Sorry.

314
00:15:48.949 --> 00:15:51.429
That's okay. Everybody does it.
Nothing to be ashamed of.

315
00:15:56.457 --> 00:15:59.217
Hank? Oh, Hank. There you are.

316
00:16:00.044 --> 00:16:02.544
Wow. You got us out of there.

317
00:16:03.213 --> 00:16:05.383
Huh. I did.

318
00:16:07.092 --> 00:16:08.382
I got us out of there.

319
00:16:09.345 --> 00:16:11.105
I mean, technically
you also got us in there.

320
00:16:11.513 --> 00:16:14.683
But if you hadn't I'm not sure
we would have gotten here.

321
00:16:17.227 --> 00:16:20.197
Echolocation. Echolocation!

322
00:16:20.356 --> 00:16:23.776
The world's most powerful pair
of glasses. We found it!

323
00:16:23.901 --> 00:16:26.021
No. You found that.

324
00:16:31.533 --> 00:16:34.163
Welcome to the Open Ocean.

325
00:16:35.162 --> 00:16:36.242
Home.

326
00:16:38.749 --> 00:16:43.499
Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo, ooo-roo.
Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo.

327
00:16:43.629 --> 00:16:45.589
Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo. Ooo-roo, ooo-roo!

328
00:16:45.756 --> 00:16:47.426
Dad, stop. She's not coming back.

329
00:16:47.591 --> 00:16:49.051
She might. Ooo-roo, ooo-roo!

330
00:16:49.134 --> 00:16:51.264
Dad! You made her feel like
she couldn't do it.

331
00:16:58.352 --> 00:17:00.352
You're not talking about Becky, are you?

332
00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:04.060
I miss Dory.

333
00:17:04.692 --> 00:17:05.942
Me too.

334
00:17:10.364 --> 00:17:12.954
The truth is,
I'm just so worried about her.

335
00:17:13.701 --> 00:17:15.531
She's the one who should be worried
about us.

336
00:17:16.203 --> 00:17:19.203
Well, she would definitely have an idea
of what to do if she were here.

337
00:17:20.124 --> 00:17:21.544
I don't know how she does that.

338
00:17:21.709 --> 00:17:25.539
I don't think she knows, Dad.
She just does.

339
00:17:25.713 --> 00:17:28.383
Well, then we'll just have to think.

340
00:17:29.717 --> 00:17:32.057
- What would Dory do?
- What would Dory do?

341
00:17:32.219 --> 00:17:34.129
Yeah! What would Dory do?

342
00:17:34.805 --> 00:17:37.605
She would assess her situation,
and then she'd evaluate...

343
00:17:37.766 --> 00:17:39.476
then she would analyse her options...

344
00:17:39.643 --> 00:17:42.233
Dad, that's "what would Marlin do."

345
00:17:42.354 --> 00:17:44.754
Right, that's what I would do.
She wouldn't even think twice.

346
00:17:44.898 --> 00:17:47.018
She would just look at the first thing
she sees and...

347
00:17:59.747 --> 00:18:00.917
Dory would do it.

348
00:18:02.833 --> 00:18:03.833
Mmm.

349
00:18:04.626 --> 00:18:06.836
Nemo, hold on to me.

350
00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:07.920
Whoa!

351
00:18:10.466 --> 00:18:11.676
Whoo-hoo!

352
00:18:11.759 --> 00:18:12.959
Hey, it's working! Whoa!

353
00:18:18.724 --> 00:18:22.434
Just keep gasping.

354
00:18:28.442 --> 00:18:30.982
- Are you okay?
- Yeah! What would Dory do now?

355
00:18:31.153 --> 00:18:32.193
Who's Dory?

356
00:18:33.489 --> 00:18:35.609
Oh boy. Are we happy to see you.

357
00:18:35.699 --> 00:18:38.029
Happy to see me? I'm happy to see you!

358
00:18:38.202 --> 00:18:40.832
I haven't had anyone to talk to in years.

359
00:18:40.996 --> 00:18:42.666
Years? Wow.

360
00:18:42.748 --> 00:18:45.018
Unfortunately we can't stay long.
We have to go because...

361
00:18:45.042 --> 00:18:47.672
Now why would you want to go?
You just landed.

362
00:18:47.836 --> 00:18:50.796
Stay a while. Tell me all about yourself.

363
00:18:50.964 --> 00:18:53.674
I would love to, but my son and I
have to get to quarantine, so...

364
00:18:53.842 --> 00:18:55.882
- Wonderful thing to have a son.
- Yeah it is.

365
00:18:56.053 --> 00:18:59.143
Of course I don't have a family.
I dated a nice scallop for a while.

366
00:18:59.306 --> 00:19:01.284
- That's fascinating, but...
- But scallops have eyes.

367
00:19:01.308 --> 00:19:03.495
And she was looking for something
different. I'm kidding!

368
00:19:03.519 --> 00:19:05.479
Well, not about scallops having eyes.
They do.

369
00:19:05.646 --> 00:19:07.896
And they see into your soul
and they break your heart.

370
00:19:08.065 --> 00:19:12.405
Oh, Shelley! Why? Why?

371
00:19:12.569 --> 00:19:13.899
Now what would Dory do?

372
00:19:15.239 --> 00:19:17.159
Come with us as we explore

373
00:19:17.741 --> 00:19:20.661
the mysterious world
of the Open Ocean.

374
00:19:22.371 --> 00:19:24.831
- Okay, Hank, follow me.
- You're in a cup.

375
00:19:24.998 --> 00:19:26.418
Right. I'll follow you then.

376
00:19:38.679 --> 00:19:41.679
- Wait.
- An octopus has three hearts.

377
00:19:42.891 --> 00:19:44.291
Huh. That's a fun fact.

378
00:19:54.903 --> 00:19:56.783
We're here.
This is really happening.

379
00:19:56.863 --> 00:19:57.943
Sh!

380
00:20:08.417 --> 00:20:11.927
Well, looks like this is it, kid.
Now I got a truck to catch.

381
00:20:12.087 --> 00:20:14.427
Wait! Wait! I had something for you.

382
00:20:16.925 --> 00:20:20.225
- Tag.
- The tag. Right!

383
00:20:27.102 --> 00:20:30.392
You know,
I think I'm gonna remember you.

384
00:20:33.066 --> 00:20:35.236
Oh, you'll forget me in a heartbeat, kid.

385
00:20:35.736 --> 00:20:36.986
Three heartbeats.

386
00:20:38.322 --> 00:20:40.042
I'll have a hard time
forgetting you though.

387
00:20:45.412 --> 00:20:47.122
My parents are actually down there.

388
00:20:51.627 --> 00:20:52.717
Um...

389
00:20:52.794 --> 00:20:53.924
You okay?

390
00:20:55.422 --> 00:20:56.422
I'm ready.

391
00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.920
Yeah, I think you are.

392
00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:01.260
Whoa!

393
00:21:05.932 --> 00:21:07.102
Wow!

394
00:21:10.979 --> 00:21:15.099
Where are they? Where are they?
Where are they? Okay. Okay.

395
00:21:20.781 --> 00:21:25.911
Pardon me. Oh. Hi. Hello. Have you
seen a mom and a dad without me?

396
00:21:26.078 --> 00:21:27.838
Excuse me. Have you seen a couple?

397
00:21:27.913 --> 00:21:29.193
They're old like you.

398
00:21:29.289 --> 00:21:31.829
Not old like you,
but older than you even.

399
00:21:31.917 --> 00:21:32.967
Okay. Bye.

400
00:21:33.126 --> 00:21:38.296
Hi. Do you know anyone who lost a kid
a long time ago that would be me?

401
00:21:38.465 --> 00:21:41.595
I don't know how long ago exact...
Okay. You're in a hurry.

402
00:21:41.718 --> 00:21:43.938
- Ho, ho! Watch where you're going.
- Oh sorry.

403
00:21:50.936 --> 00:21:54.526
It's our goal that every
animal we rescue and care for...

404
00:21:54.690 --> 00:21:57.150
will eventually return home
to where they belong.

405
00:22:02.155 --> 00:22:03.325
Shells.

406
00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:07.450
And there we go.
Now, if you ever get lost, Dory...

407
00:22:07.619 --> 00:22:09.369
You just follow the shells.

408
00:22:09.538 --> 00:22:10.998
Hey, look! Shells!

409
00:22:18.672 --> 00:22:20.632
Follow the shells.

410
00:22:32.519 --> 00:22:35.309
- Hey, I live there.
- Yes, yes indeed.

411
00:22:36.398 --> 00:22:38.818
My home. That's my home!

412
00:22:40.193 --> 00:22:41.983
Mom! Dad!

413
00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:46.200
Okay, kelpcake. Now count to ten.

414
00:22:47.075 --> 00:22:49.705
1, 2, 3...

415
00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:51.950
4...

416
00:22:52.539 --> 00:22:54.869
You're welcome.

417
00:22:55.041 --> 00:22:56.751
Who are you talking to, kelpcake?

418
00:22:56.918 --> 00:22:58.678
My pipe pal, Destiny!

419
00:23:03.049 --> 00:23:05.549
Mom? Dad?

420
00:23:14.728 --> 00:23:16.438
Mommy loves purple shells.

421
00:23:24.529 --> 00:23:28.069
- Mommy?
- What's going to happen to her?

422
00:23:28.241 --> 00:23:29.991
There, there, Jenny.

423
00:23:30.577 --> 00:23:33.167
Oh no, don't cry, Mommy. Don't cry.

424
00:23:33.246 --> 00:23:36.336
Do you think she's... That she can
make it on her own, Charlie?

425
00:23:36.416 --> 00:23:39.376
Oh, honey. It'll be okay.

426
00:23:42.088 --> 00:23:43.928
Mommy loves purple shells.

427
00:23:54.434 --> 00:23:55.724
- Dory!
- Dory?

428
00:23:55.894 --> 00:23:57.484
- Dory!
- Mommy?

429
00:23:58.730 --> 00:24:01.560
- Dory!
- Mommy! Daddy!

430
00:24:04.736 --> 00:24:06.156
My parents...

431
00:24:07.447 --> 00:24:09.657
I... I lost them.

432
00:24:18.124 --> 00:24:19.964
It was my fault.

433
00:24:20.961 --> 00:24:22.631
- Where's your tag?
- Huh?

434
00:24:22.796 --> 00:24:26.596
Your tag. It's missing.
That why you're not in quarantine?

435
00:24:26.716 --> 00:24:27.886
- Quarantine?
- Yeah!

436
00:24:28.009 --> 00:24:31.129
That's where they took all
the blue tangs. Isn't that right, Bill?

437
00:24:31.304 --> 00:24:34.304
Yep. The blue tangs are getting
their own exhibit in Cleveland.

438
00:24:34.474 --> 00:24:37.644
Being shipped out on a truck
at the crack of dawn. Must be nice.

439
00:24:37.769 --> 00:24:40.099
What? No! No, my parents
are back in quarantine?

440
00:24:40.272 --> 00:24:43.022
They're being shipped to Cleveland?
But I just got here!

441
00:24:43.191 --> 00:24:45.002
I've got to get to them.
They don't know I'm here.

442
00:24:45.026 --> 00:24:47.486
Don't worry,
it's easy to get to quarantine.

443
00:24:47.654 --> 00:24:49.324
You can just go through the pipes,
honey.

444
00:24:51.658 --> 00:24:54.248
Oh. Oh I can't do that.

445
00:24:54.953 --> 00:24:57.453
- Why not?
- I'll forget where I'm going.

446
00:24:57.622 --> 00:25:00.792
And I can't be somewhere
where I have nobody to help me.

447
00:25:00.959 --> 00:25:03.829
- Well, then I guess you're stuck here.
- You're not helping, Bill.

448
00:25:04.004 --> 00:25:06.504
Just go in there if you want to.
You'll be fine.

449
00:25:10.427 --> 00:25:11.637
Oh boy.

450
00:25:12.220 --> 00:25:16.140
Could you tell me how to get there?
Through the pipes?

451
00:25:16.308 --> 00:25:20.318
Sure, honey. It's two lefts
and then a right. Simple.

452
00:25:24.316 --> 00:25:25.816
Okay.

453
00:25:28.028 --> 00:25:30.698
Two lefts and a right. I can do this.

454
00:25:30.864 --> 00:25:33.704
Two lefts and a right. Okay.
Don't forget.

455
00:25:39.539 --> 00:25:41.499
Two lefts and a right.
Two lefts and a right.

456
00:25:42.584 --> 00:25:46.544
Two lefts and a right. Two lefts
and a right. Two lefts and a right.

457
00:25:48.423 --> 00:25:52.383
Two lefts and a right? Shoot.

458
00:25:53.595 --> 00:25:57.515
Left and a right. Wait.
Did I already take a left?

459
00:25:57.641 --> 00:26:02.021
Oh no. It's happening. Okay, hold on.
Hold on, hold on, hold on.

460
00:26:02.145 --> 00:26:06.065
Which way? Where am I going?
I can't remember. Okay.

461
00:26:06.232 --> 00:26:07.877
Okay. I'm lost. It's too hard.
I can't remember.

462
00:26:07.901 --> 00:26:09.071
I'm forgetting everything.

463
00:26:09.235 --> 00:26:13.075
I'm gonna be stuck forever in the pipes.
The pipes! The pipe pals.

464
00:26:13.198 --> 00:26:15.748
Pipe pals? Pipe pals!

465
00:26:15.909 --> 00:26:19.449
- And... swim, swim, swim.
- Yeah, I don't know about this.

466
00:26:19.621 --> 00:26:21.991
Trust me,
I won't let you hit anything. Wall!

467
00:26:23.208 --> 00:26:25.128
What's the point?
I'll never learn to get around!

468
00:26:25.210 --> 00:26:28.022
You better! If you can't do it in here
you'll never do it out in the ocean.

469
00:26:28.046 --> 00:26:30.296
Now really focus, okay? Wall!

470
00:26:30.465 --> 00:26:31.965
Destiny!

471
00:26:32.133 --> 00:26:33.923
Dory? Hello?

472
00:26:34.094 --> 00:26:37.804
I'm lost in the pipes
and my parents are in quarantine!

473
00:26:37.973 --> 00:26:41.313
Hang on, Dory! Bailey!
You've got to use your echolocation!

474
00:26:41.476 --> 00:26:42.316
You know it's broken!

475
00:26:42.477 --> 00:26:45.039
Just stop it, and try the "Ooh" thing
Dory talked about, will you?

476
00:26:45.063 --> 00:26:47.263
- But I don't think I can...
- Don't bail on me, Bailey!

477
00:26:48.191 --> 00:26:51.151
Ooh!

478
00:26:52.404 --> 00:26:53.614
Ooh! Ooh!

479
00:26:53.780 --> 00:26:56.780
Come on, Bailey. What did you
just tell me, huh? Really focus!

480
00:26:56.950 --> 00:26:58.320
Ooh! I feel stupid.

481
00:26:58.493 --> 00:27:00.623
- Bailey.
- Sorry. Ooh!

482
00:27:00.787 --> 00:27:02.247
- Hello?
- Here!

483
00:27:02.330 --> 00:27:04.290
We're here!

484
00:27:04.457 --> 00:27:08.087
- Guys... Ooh! Guys... Ooh!
- What? What is it?

485
00:27:08.169 --> 00:27:12.379
I'm getting something! Ooh!
Here we go! Ooh! Oh yes! Ooh!

486
00:27:13.008 --> 00:27:17.138
I can see the quarantine!
This is amazing!

487
00:27:17.262 --> 00:27:21.222
Ooh! I can see everything!
And I can see you!

488
00:27:21.307 --> 00:27:23.107
He can see you!

489
00:27:23.268 --> 00:27:25.188
My life's a rainbow! Can you see me?

490
00:27:25.270 --> 00:27:27.350
Right,
it doesn't work that way.

491
00:27:27.522 --> 00:27:29.652
- Bailey!
- Okay! Tell Dory to go left!

492
00:27:29.816 --> 00:27:31.196
He says go left!

493
00:27:31.359 --> 00:27:32.729
Left?

494
00:27:34.362 --> 00:27:36.572
- Ooh! Straight!
- Straight!

495
00:27:36.656 --> 00:27:38.496
- Straight!
- Ooh! Go right!

496
00:27:38.658 --> 00:27:40.328
- Right!
- Right!

497
00:27:41.161 --> 00:27:44.201
Ooh! I'm light-headed! Ooh! Wait. Ooh!

498
00:27:44.372 --> 00:27:46.662
I'm picking up something else.
Hold on! Let me zoom out.

499
00:27:46.750 --> 00:27:48.410
Zzz...

500
00:27:48.501 --> 00:27:50.621
Holy Neptune, she's not alone! Ooh!

501
00:27:50.712 --> 00:27:52.832
- What is it?
- I can't tell! But it's coming for her.

502
00:27:52.922 --> 00:27:56.512
Oh no! Dory, swim!
Swim the other way!

503
00:27:56.676 --> 00:27:58.096
- What? Where?
- What? Where?

504
00:27:58.219 --> 00:27:59.759
- Go right!
- Right!

505
00:28:01.765 --> 00:28:04.185
No, my right!
Oh no! She's heading right towards it!

506
00:28:04.350 --> 00:28:06.180
No! Dory, turn around!

507
00:28:08.021 --> 00:28:10.521
That's great, Dory!
You're headed right toward us!

508
00:28:10.690 --> 00:28:12.350
What? You want me to go right?

509
00:28:12.484 --> 00:28:13.944
No! No! Not right. Oh, I can't look!

510
00:28:18.198 --> 00:28:19.708
- Dory!
- Marlin?

511
00:28:19.824 --> 00:28:21.343
- I knew it! You're okay!
- Oh my gosh!

512
00:28:21.367 --> 00:28:25.207
It's consuming her!
It's eating her alive!

513
00:28:26.873 --> 00:28:29.373
- You're okay!
- You found me! How did you find me?

514
00:28:29.542 --> 00:28:31.712
There was a crazy clam.
He wouldn't stop talking.

515
00:28:31.878 --> 00:28:35.048
We just slowly backed away from him
and into these pipes.

516
00:28:35.215 --> 00:28:36.715
And then we just started looking.

517
00:28:36.883 --> 00:28:39.553
Dory! I'm sorry!

518
00:28:39.719 --> 00:28:41.219
Okay, what was that?

519
00:28:41.387 --> 00:28:42.727
Hang on. I got to take this.

520
00:28:42.889 --> 00:28:45.599
It's okay! Sorry for what?

521
00:28:45.725 --> 00:28:47.725
What? You're okay?

522
00:28:47.894 --> 00:28:49.414
- Yes!
- I found Marlin and Nemo!

523
00:28:50.563 --> 00:28:53.273
Dad! Did you hear that?
Dory really does speak whale.

524
00:28:53.441 --> 00:28:54.521
I heard.

525
00:28:54.609 --> 00:28:57.249
It's bringing back some very bad
memories so let's get out of here.

526
00:28:57.362 --> 00:29:01.202
I say we go this way.
Follow me. It's time to head home!

527
00:29:01.741 --> 00:29:05.161
Wait, wait, wait! Um...
My parents are here.

528
00:29:05.286 --> 00:29:07.086
- They are?
- You found your parents?

529
00:29:07.247 --> 00:29:11.587
Well, not exactly. No. I mean not yet,
but, um, I know where they are.

530
00:29:11.751 --> 00:29:16.041
I don't know exactly how to get there,
but I know that... I'm getting help...

531
00:29:16.214 --> 00:29:17.934
- Down to quarantine.
- Quarantine.

532
00:29:18.091 --> 00:29:21.761
That's it! Oh, and I met
this septopus, super cranky...

533
00:29:21.928 --> 00:29:26.938
but secretly kind of sweet, and he
got me into the exhibit... The exhibit.

534
00:29:29.435 --> 00:29:30.435
Dory?

535
00:29:31.271 --> 00:29:33.441
Do you think my parents
will want to see me?

536
00:29:33.606 --> 00:29:35.946
What? Why wouldn't they
want to see you?

537
00:29:36.776 --> 00:29:39.946
Because... I lost them?

538
00:29:40.947 --> 00:29:44.917
Dory, your parents are going to be
overjoyed to see you.

539
00:29:45.743 --> 00:29:48.783
They're going to have missed...
everything about you.

540
00:29:48.955 --> 00:29:51.295
- Really?
- Do you know how we found you?

541
00:29:51.457 --> 00:29:53.297
- Something about a clam? Or...
- No.

542
00:29:53.459 --> 00:29:54.289
- No, an oyster.
- No.

543
00:29:54.460 --> 00:29:55.500
- Mollusc?
- No.

544
00:29:55.670 --> 00:29:56.330
- Something?
- No.

545
00:29:56.504 --> 00:29:57.754
- I don't... No?
- No clam.

546
00:29:57.922 --> 00:30:00.632
We were having a very hard time
until Nemo thought...

547
00:30:00.800 --> 00:30:02.800
"What would Dory do?"

548
00:30:03.386 --> 00:30:04.636
Why would you say that?

549
00:30:04.804 --> 00:30:07.804
Because ever since I've met you,
you've shown me how to do...

550
00:30:07.974 --> 00:30:12.184
stuff I never dreamed of doing.
Crazy things!

551
00:30:13.021 --> 00:30:16.521
Outsmarting sharks
and jumping jellyfish.

552
00:30:17.692 --> 00:30:21.982
And finding my son.
You made all that happen.

553
00:30:23.198 --> 00:30:28.038
Really? I didn't know you thought that.
Unless I forgot.

554
00:30:29.287 --> 00:30:32.497
No, you didn't forget. I never told you.

555
00:30:33.833 --> 00:30:35.503
And I'm sorry about that.

556
00:30:37.795 --> 00:30:43.635
But, Dory, because of who you are,
you are about to find your parents.

557
00:30:45.637 --> 00:30:51.187
And when you do that, you'll be home.

558
00:31:03.696 --> 00:31:05.196
Dad.

559
00:31:05.365 --> 00:31:08.415
Does this mean
we have to say goodbye to Dory?

560
00:31:10.328 --> 00:31:12.378
Yes, Nemo. We do.
